{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: archive input-work fix at exact head 7c8103c7db22a6b38cfb550a123ceae9bb02f851, tree 2bfc8f35cc977efd1a92f453c68334b16271b5af (review request b68b7337, promise 54451051, implementation 78638def / ade43f69). It satisfies request 78638def as amended by planner ruling 6178a623, its evidence is adequate, and it may land. Deployment is planner-owned.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-23-archive-input-work.md (artifact 73a266af), first and in full. Then I read the production diff (packages/git/src/http-read.ts, packages/scope/src/archive-host.ts), the tests (http-read.test.ts, archive-host.test.ts, the new archive-input-work.test.ts), the seal map and the tracked evidence.\n\nWhat the head changes.\n- An isolated v2 parent read now reserves only fixed work before I/O: 2 calls, 1,024 metadata and 1,024 input work.\n- Payload work is charged at 32 units per byte at the actual work boundaries, through a trusted synchronous reserveWork callback:\n  - each wire chunk, in readBytes after the existing size check and before its owned copy, for both the advertisement and the upload response;\n  - each pack entry's declared inflated size, in decodePack after the existing type and aggregate inflation checks and before zlibEnd and decompression;\n  - each delta result size, in applyDelta after its existing limit check and before allocation.\n- The actual-count reservation (1,024 per object), the generic reader's 4 × maximum, v0 behaviour, the wanted-only cache, deadlines and all ARCHIVE_BOUNDS caps are unchanged.\n- A refused admission keeps its exact budget error through readBytes, #request and the object read, and it abandons the source so it cannot be reused.\n\nChecks against ruling 6178a623.\n- Partial progress, receipt and drain: the new Native test seeds one commit, at most 745 tree bytes and at most 6 blobs (measured 529 and 4). A 300-checkpoint backlog then drains over several confirmed passes. The first pass is