n hook makes the v2 case fail with a zlib-header refusal instead of the exact quota error. Restoring the old maximum debit makes the Native preplanning assertion fail at 51,635,300 against a ceiling of 16,777,216. Both show that the tests can tell the change apart from its absence.\n5. Seal: the only seal change is packages/scope/src/archive-host.ts, now 94914ff2…3249673, the value of the recorded seal run. The gate's Node block, which includes security-entry-points.test.mjs, passed with it.\n6. Document checks at this head: git diff --check -B against b1b2169c is clean. check-commit-messages reports 10 checked, 0 flagged. Section citations report 1,876 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved; the citation script is identical to Main's.\n\nArchitecture: the charge moves from an up-front tariff based on the read's maximum to staged admission at the real work boundaries, inside the existing Git transport and Scope adapter. No new layer, port, I/O, fallback or retry is added. The worst case per read can now exceed the old fixed tariff, because wire, inflation and delta work are each charged, but the unchanged per-pass caps still bound the whole pass.\nSecurity: I found no defect. Each reservation runs before the work it pays for. Every size is checked against its existing bound before the charge. The callback is type-checked and forwarded only on isolated v2 reads. A refusal is terminal for that source and keeps its exact error. No provider error text is newly exposed. Received chunks were already bounded by maxBytes before admission.\nSimplification: one small WorkAdmission class and three call sites. Comments explain the order. The test is long, but it states its fixture limits and assertions directly.\n\nFindings: none.\n\nResidual risk: these are local fixture results, not hosted ones. The P2 tree-byte ceiling remains, and Room A may stall at 8,487 tree bytes during its catch-up. Ruling 6178a623 accepts that, with fc2548ae to follow. Nine hosted \"unavailable\" passes remain unexplained, as the note says; the planner's post-deploy tail should show whether they persist.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:73a266afa092d9f2c02713edc70d9fefbd3767e9","binding":"assigned","head":"7c8103c7db22a6b38cfb550a123ceae9bb02f851","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:54451051e8bc742d56fdc3a93b2e52ebc2a7da26\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ade43f6922e44f5f7366ae8ba9bdb53206bbc645\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f31f0a0d852e680c75596b0c9d5eb137d5705050","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}